WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.870
-Yesterday we saw one of
the most extraordinarily moments

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.506
of Donald Trump's presidency
when the FBI raided the offices

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.374
of personal lawyer
Michael Cohen,

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.910
and in response, Trump
has completely lost his mind.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.945
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.647 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:17.083 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.386
It's hard to imagine how
Donald Trump could be in

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.321
more legal jeopardy
than he is right now.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:25.892
Basically, Trump has more legal
problems than Conor McGregor

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.861
and just as many concussions.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.362
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.598
And yet somehow things got
much worse yesterday for Trump.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:34.734
-Tonight, a dramatic FBI raid

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.502
at the New York office
and hotel room

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:37.603
of Michael Cohen,

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:39.339
The President's
personal attorney

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:42.675
who paid off adult film star
Stormy Daniels for her silence

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.777
about alleged affair
with Mr. Trump.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:45.678
-"The New York Times" also

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.380
reporting that the FBI also

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.848
seized e-mails, tax documents,

00:00:49.848 --> 00:00:51.384
and business records,

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.785
and that the records include

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:54.320
communications between

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.354
Michael Cohen,

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:56.255
The President's attorney,

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:57.757
and President Trump.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.826
-Federal Prosecutors
in Manhattan obtained

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.895
search warrants after a referral

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.596
from special counsel
Robert Mueller,

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.399
who found evidence
of a potential crime.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.800
-Wow, so, just to recap,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.670
the FBI, an organization Trump
has attacked for months,

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.238
raided the office
of Michael Cohen,

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.639
his longtime personal fixer,

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:16.376
and seized tax documents,
which he has repeatedly refused

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:19.311
to release related
to campaign finance violations

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:21.180
during the election involving
Stormy Daniels,

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.115
the porn star he allegedly
had an affair with,

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:24.784
on a referral from
Robert Mueller,

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.719
the special counsel
in the Russia investigation.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:30.723
This is like the series finale
of a TV show

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.793
where they try to tie all the
different plot lines together.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:38.597
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:39.999
You're watching like, "Oh!

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.901
It's Michael Cohen
from season one!

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.905
What's he doing in this episode?
Ohhhhh!"

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.674
If Trump ever goes on trial,
they're gonna call characters

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:50.410
from previous episodes
into the courtroom

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.378
like the last episode
of "Seinfeld."

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.512
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:55.013
[ As Trump ]
"Oh, no, Anthony Scaramucci,

00:01:55.013 --> 00:01:57.249
what did I do to you?"

00:01:57.249 --> 00:01:58.318
[ Deep voice ]
"No Mooch for you."

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.718
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:01.620
[ Normal voice ] Of course,
when news like this breaks,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.224
we can always count on
our calm, rational president

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:05.991
to react in a measured way,

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:08.160
and he once again rose
to the occasion this morning

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.996
when he got up bright and early
and tweeted

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.365
these reassuring words
to a nation in turmoil...

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:15.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.403
And then,
less than a minute later,

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.472
he added this helpful
follow-up...

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.741
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.677
So the Feds seize Trump's
communications with his lawyers,

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.612
and the next morning,
Trump woke up and screamed

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:28.481
"Attorney-client privilege
is dead!"

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.116
What is Trump's strategy here,

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:33.653
to act so guilty the feds will
think he has to be innocent?

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:34.487
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.055
You know, the insanity defense

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.858
only works after
you've been arrested, right?

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.559
[ As Trump ] They can't
arrest me if I'm crazy.

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:43.195
Quick, somebody get me a diaper
I can wear as a hat.

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:48.768
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.202
[ Normal voice ] Now,
Michael Cohen isn't just

00:02:50.202 --> 00:02:52.137
a peripheral player
in Trump's world.

00:02:52.137 --> 00:02:53.973
He's been Trump's loyal fixer
for years,

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.674
and he's as close
to Trump's inner circle

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:56.909
as you can possibly get.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:59.478
And last month,
as the controversy surrounding

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:01.747
the Stormy Daniels story
was intensifying,

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:04.183
Cohen insisted that
he would remain forever loyal

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:06.819 line:0%
to his boss and that the
hush payment he allegedly paid

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.588 line:0%
went beyond politics.
He told "Vanity Fair"...

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:28.073
Yeah, just a thing a friend
does for a friend.

00:03:28.073 --> 00:03:29.776
Like when your buddy forgets
his wallet,

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:32.311
so you pay for his coffee,
except instead of coffee,

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:34.714
it's a porn star, and instead
of forgetting his wallet,

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.415
he forgot his wedding vows.

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:40.620
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.657
And say what you will
about Donald Trump,

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.326
but he's a man who respects
and appreciates loyalty.

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.495
A friend like that deserves
nothing less

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.263
than mutual admiration
and devotion.

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:53.132
So naturally Trump
did what he does

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:55.000
to all of his most loyal
servants --

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.503
he immediately threw him
under the bus.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.955
-That's right.
He said "Ask Michael Cohen."

00:04:16.955 --> 00:04:19.092
And it looks like the FBI said,
"Okay."

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.760
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.896
Now, suffice to say the fact
that federal prosecutors

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.298
obtained a warrant to raid
the offices of The President's

00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:28.167
personal attorney
and seize communications

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.935
with The President
is a huge deal.

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:32.671
It's incredibly rare and must
meet a high legal burden.

00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:35.174
While the exact details of
the warrant are still unknown,

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:37.543
yesterday, we started to learn
more about which

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:40.380
potential crimes investigators
might be looking into.

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:51.524
-Wow! It's amazing how many
different crimes the Trump team

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:52.725
has been able to cover.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.326
You got Michael Cohen
on bank fraud,

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:56.662
wire fraud,
and campaign finance violations,

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:59.198
Paul Manafort on failing to
register as a foreign agent,

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:01.200
Michael Flynn
on lying to the FBI,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.970
and Jared Kushner for, I don't
know, probably using a fake ID.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.138
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.171
[ High-pitched, raspy voice ]
Hi, I'm 21.

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:07.206
I work at the White House.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:10.543
I'd like to buy some beer,
please.

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:13.445
Do you have to buy six,
or can you get one or two?

00:05:13.445 --> 00:05:15.581
[ Normal voice ] And here's a
fun fact I learned yesterday --

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.583
Michael Cohen's office,
the one that was raided

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:21.220
by the FBI, is actually located
at 30 Rockefeller Plaza.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.256
That's the building
we are in right now,

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:25.324
The one we tape this show
in every day.

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:27.493
I feel like Dorothy
in "The Wizard of Oz."

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:31.530
Everything I was looking for was
right there with me all along.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.937
Michael Cohen was very much
the keeper

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.772
of Trump's
most closely held secrets,

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.773
and the fact that FBI
raided his office

00:05:41.773 --> 00:05:43.910
and seized his communications
with Trump is being taken

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.311
by outside lawyers as a sign

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.046
of just how serious
the investigation is.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.082
One lawyer told
"The Washington Post"...

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.263
And if there's anyone
who knows the worst about Trump,

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:05.598
it's his barber.

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:07.233
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:11.470
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.673
Cohen may very well know
more about Donald Trump

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:16.109
than any other being
on the planet,

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:18.377
which might explain why in
his first comments to the media

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:19.879
yesterday after the story broke,

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:21.413
Trump seemed to come
totally unglued.

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:24.116
He was supposed to meet
with his national security team

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:24.950
to discuss Syria,

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:26.585
but completely unprompted,

00:06:26.585 --> 00:06:27.619
he began the meeting

00:06:27.619 --> 00:06:29.188
by attacking the FBI.

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:31.190
-So, I just heard that they

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.126
broke into the office of

00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:36.229
one of my personal attorneys.

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:38.964
-They broke in? They're the FBI.

00:06:38.964 --> 00:06:40.733
They had a search warrant.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:43.302
That's like waking up from
surgery and telling your doctor,

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:46.272
"You stole my appendix!"

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:49.808
Trump once again aired one of
his long-simmering grievances,

00:06:49.808 --> 00:06:51.844
his anger at Attorney General
Jeff Sessions,

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:53.979
who recused himself
from the Russia investigation

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:56.048
because he has misled Congress

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:57.282
and because he had been a part

00:06:57.282 --> 00:06:59.251
of the campaign that was
being investigated.

00:06:59.251 --> 00:07:02.521 line:0%
Trump wants someone in charge
who will exert influence

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:04.557 line:0%
over the probe and potentially
shut it down,

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.658 line:0%
and he made that clear again
yesterday.

00:07:06.658 --> 00:07:07.693
-The Attorney General made

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:10.128
a terrible mistake when

00:07:10.128 --> 00:07:12.231
he did this and when he recused

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:13.432
himself, or he should have

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:14.967
certainly let us know if he was

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:16.602
going to recuse himself

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:19.071
and would have put a different

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.539
Attorney General in.

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:22.941
-I shudder to imagine who else
Trump would have named

00:07:22.941 --> 00:07:24.009
as Attorney General --

00:07:24.009 --> 00:07:26.412
Chris Christie, Rudy Giuliani,

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:29.181
an Amazon Echo
that only watches Fox News.

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:31.149
-[ Amazon Echo voice] Hillary.
Obama. Deep state. Witch hunt.

00:07:31.149 --> 00:07:33.018
E-mails. E-mails. E-mails.
E-mails. E-mails. E-mails.

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:34.119
E-mails. E-mails.
E-mails. E-mails.

00:07:34.119 --> 00:07:35.421
-Heeey!

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:37.723
Trump was so panicked
and flustered when he spoke

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:40.192
to the media that he just
kept mindlessly repeating

00:07:40.192 --> 00:07:42.261
the same words over and over.

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:43.963
-It's a disgraceful situation.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:44.830
-It's a disgrace.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.365
It's frankly a real disgrace.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:47.466
I think it's a disgrace.

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:49.568
It's a disgrace.
It's a disgrace.

00:07:49.568 --> 00:07:50.836
I think it's a disgrace.

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:52.405
I think it's disgraceful.

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:54.941
It's a disgrace.

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:55.874
[ Laughter ]

00:07:55.874 --> 00:07:56.976
-Hey, man, if you are not

00:07:56.976 --> 00:07:58.844
going to bother to read
the Constitution,

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:00.947
could you at least check out
a thesaurus?

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:02.281
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:04.717
[ As Trump ] You look at
what's going on, it's...

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:06.251
ignominious.

00:08:06.251 --> 00:08:07.419
[ Normal voice ] Oh. Okay.

00:08:07.419 --> 00:08:10.522
We'll give you credit for that.

00:08:10.522 --> 00:08:13.191
One of the most unsettling
things about Trump's comments

00:08:13.191 --> 00:08:15.461
was they were made at a meeting
where Trump was supposed

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:18.097
to be deciding whether to use
military force against Syria.

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:19.398
In fact, sitting next to him

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:22.267
was his new National Security
Advisor John Bolton.

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:25.404
And Trump noted the awkward
timing of his arrival.

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:26.672
-John, I want to thank you
very much.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:29.408
This is gonna be a lot of work.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:30.876
Interesting day. He picked today

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:33.246
as his first day, so, Generals,

00:08:33.246 --> 00:08:34.946
I think he picked the right day.

00:08:34.946 --> 00:08:35.982
-No, he didn't.

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:37.016
[ Laughter ]

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.684
This is like starting your job

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:41.654
at Enron on the day
of the crash.

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:44.557
"Oh, you must be the new guy.
Here, grab a shredder."

00:08:44.557 --> 00:08:46.859
[ Laughter ]

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:48.327 line:0%
This is one of the most
consequential

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:50.796 line:0%
and potentially most perilous
moments in the Trump presidency.

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:53.699 line:0%
One of his closest confidants is
in the cross hairs of the FBI,

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:55.835
and he's openly threatening
to shut down

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:57.470
the special counsel's
investigation.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.205
And if that happens,
I can think of at least one word

00:09:00.205 --> 00:09:02.307
I'd use to describe
the situation.

00:09:02.307 --> 00:09:03.175
-It's a disgrace.

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:04.643
Disgrace. Disgrace.

00:09:04.643 --> 00:09:06.579
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:07.646
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:07.646 --> 00:09:09.849 line:0%
♪♪

